Z||000000||rodmcneill||11-28-2000||11:37 PM||||I have been thinking about getting my windows tinted on both my GTs. After pricing local shops $220-$250 for both I was thinking about trying it myself.I am sure forum members have done this. Any tips on this? Can I expect a decent job doing it myself? Is there a brand of window film that is better than another? If I do it myself I would buy the most expensive film and an installation kit.||||reg||5
Z||000001||sqoach||11-28-2000||11:52 PM||||most tint jobs that i have seen that were done by the owner didn't come out too good.  it's tougher than you think to do a good job tinting windows.  i've tried it once and it looked ok at first, but after a while, you could see air bubbles and i just ripped it off.  and just because a kit is expensive, doesn't mean it's the best.  if you really want you windows tinted and a good job of it, i would pay a professional to do it.  that's just my opinion though.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||11-29-2000||12:25 AM||||A window tint shop did mine for $100 (all 3) with lifetime war.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||14
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||11-29-2000||12:36 AM||||is mirror tint legal in canada?<P>my local canadian tire sells it..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000004||FieroLisa||11-29-2000||01:20 AM||||I tinted the windows myself on the coupe...it didn't look bad...but it didn't look professional either. It only cost me, oh, under $20 so I guess if you have the time to waste and a lot of extra tint, you could do it yourself.<BR>BTW I ended up getting them professionally done later when my friend started doing it and gave me a deal ($40 all  windows)<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/||||reg||1
Z||000005||olympic||11-29-2000||03:56 AM||||Darklord,<BR>   That mirror tint is most likely illegal.  Here in SK they only allow you to tint the windows behind the front seats.  If you know your doctor well you can get him to give you a waiver saying that your eyes or skin are sensetive to sunlight and then you can tint all the windows as dark as you want.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||overlord||11-29-2000||09:06 AM||||i had my windows tinted  limo black...I'm in canada. The cops  pulled me over and told me  to take it off.  (side windows). I did a really good job too....grrr.....<P>The cop said you can't tint the windows if it is a film you put on.<BR>Only the rear window.||||reg||1
Z||000007||GarethWright||11-29-2000||08:24 PM||||Hi, I believe mirror tint is illegal in most places (something about the cops wanting to check out our kewl interiors  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) But, a similar effect can be had using that kinda seaweed colored tint on the newer Lexus (I think) Cars and SUVs.  I personally will stick with black.  Here in good ole OK last I heard we're legal down to 5% and any windows except windshield can be fully covered.  But I know a guy who has Really dark tint on his car, and he says its a real pain to see through at night.  sure looks kewl in the daytime though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroLisa||11-29-2000||08:31 PM||||I have 2 window tint tickets on my record. But, since they were on different cars, and they never *specifically* told me to scrape it off, well both cars are still tinted. Oh wait, ones the Subaru and that's at the junkyard now. But it's still tinted!<BR>I have all 3 windows tinted 20% on the coupe but the rear is a better tint so it looks much darker. <BR>GT will get done too- Long as they don't pull me over for any other reason, they can't just pull me over for tint (at least not in OH) Of course, in Ohio, the tint laws are something ludicrous like 50% allowed...that's barely tinted! I have friends who've gotten away with 5%.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/||||reg||1
Z||000009||robertjay||11-30-2000||12:17 AM||||Doing the tint yourself isn't too difficult if you have patience.  Make sure you are in a fairly dust free environment, maybe in a shop with a wet floor.  It needs to be fairly warm for at least a day, maybe two.  By far the best way to do it is to remove the window, but on a Fiero that is too darn tough.  For the side windows, remove the door panel and inner window seal, and make sure you get the tint below the seal.<P>On our cars it isn't too tough to make the side windows look professional, apply the film according to the instructions, and with a very, very sharp knife, trim around the edge.  Because the shape of the window, you can then move the film down about an 1/8 inch or maybe even 1/4 inch.  That ensures there is not an edge left around the window to get caught on your sleeve or something similar.<P>You may want to look into the window guides in the middle of the door.  I believe they are made of felt, or some sort of material like that.  whatever it is, it likes to attract dirt, and I believe there is one inside that can scratch the tint if it is dirty.<P>As for the rear window, I would remove as much of the interior panels as you can, to expose as much of the window as you can.  Do sort of the same trick when you trim the film, get it real close to the side and top edges, then just move the film up to get it as close to the edge of the window as possible.  I have even cut the film using a thin piece of cardboard as a pattern, cut the cardboard as close as you can to the size of the window, and you may not even have to do any trimming when applying the film.<P>One thing to keep in mind, if you have rear window defoggers, sometimes it is very difficult to get all of the air that is trapped by the heating elements, so you can lay another layer of tint, and the trapped air, if any, will be almost impossible to see, plus it'll be really dark  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>One other thing on the back window.  I have noticed on some Fiero's rear windows, there is alot of excess urethane around the edges, this will need to be cleaned with mineral spirits and a single edge razor blade.  (try not to damage the defroster if you have them).<P>Hope this helps, sorry for the long post. ||||reg||10
Z||000010||robertjay||11-30-2000||12:20 AM||||One other thing I forgot to mention above, do not, I repeat, do not roll your windows down for at least a week.  You will notice the film will look sort of hazy when you first apply it.  That is the wet glue, it will go away in a few days, and then a little while after that, the film will be dry, then you can roll the windows down.<P>Good luck.<p>[This message has been edited by robertjay (edited 11-30-2000).]||||reg||11
Z||000011||Philphine||11-30-2000||01:50 AM||||my 87 is the only car that i was able to do all the windows on since they're all pretty flat. 5% all around with a winshield band at the top and bottom. illegal but you only get a ticket if you're stopped for something else.<P>lately around here people are getting a tint that fades bettween black and silver. depending on car color it looks pretty good. i'd like to get white or mirror on my indy and something wild on my cheap fiero like the fade tint or sparkle or rainbow.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Haze_Performance||11-30-2000||02:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>I have 2 window tint tickets on my record. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Only 2?? I have 16 tickets over 5 years. So far so good, Ive never had to pay one. One of the times the officer told me to scratch the window NOW. I told him "I dont think so". He ended up giving me three tickets. (One for the tinied plate cover, One for the headlight covers & One for the windows)<P>When I moved to the burbs,I tinted the Fiero windows......... Cops here dont seem to care.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||10
Z||000013||count_iblis||11-30-2000||08:40 PM||||I have mirror tint on my eclipse and the officer next door has never said anything. (If I ever get the damn fiero fixed) I will put mirror tint on it also.  <P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||RiceCooker||12-01-2000||03:19 PM||||Here are my window tinting stories:<P>I got them tinted in the spring - back window dark side windows - light. They look great and the side indows you can still see through if you look. I did this because the rule in Alberta is no tinting unless it's behind the driver. But I'd heard from friends and other people that the cops won't bother you unless they cannot see through them. <BR>So about 2 weeks after I had them done, I'm sitting at a light and a cop pulls up behind me. Light turns green so I go (obviously not doing anything wrong) and a block later the lights go on. So I pull off the main road and he sits in his car for a while before coming up with a ticket. Blah blah blah side windows tinted etc. I even said officer they're light tint, you can see through them. Nope. So then he goes to leave and I ask him the question, "So if you were behind me how could you see my side windows?" Then he says, "Ahhh, but it's a secret." And walks off like a smarta$$ little Faggot. Needless to say I was pi$$ed off.<P>I didn't have any problems until the World Petroleum Conference or whatever was here in June or July. There was like a million cops in our city for violence precautions and they were cracking down on everything. (It put all the cops in bad moods) I'm driving home one day and I come to a 4-way stop near my house (completely residential area, nowhere near downtown) and there are 3 cops in the intersection pulling people over left and right. Sure enough, he points at me so I pull over. Now this guy was MAD! He was yelling at me for tinted side windows and got even mare upset when I tried to talk to him about it. So he says you can take that off while I write you a ticket. I just sit there and he comes back and says, "Did you here what I said?!" I said ya but I'd like to take in in to have it removed. He says No you can have it towed then! and I'm a block from my house! So i pretend to peel it off and he gives me my ticket and yells at me some more saying, "Next time this car is een on the road with tinted windows, it will be towed!"<BR>So everytime i even see a cop on the road, I roll down my windows cause I might get arrested.<BR>Is that BRUTAL or what???!!!||||reg||4
Z||000015||rogergarrison||12-01-2000||06:15 PM||||its not too hard to do yourself. cost for 3 windows is prob about $20, i think theres like 6' in a $10 box so youll need 2. I use a plastic body plastic spreader instead of what they give you (brand new only). Its pretty ez, but if you get some wrinkles that wont stay down, use a hair dryer on low setting. dont roll them down for a couple days. Also dont try to squeege the wrinkles if you get them, they will crease and you have to throw it away and start over.start by putting the straight edge on bottom edge of glass with excess all around other 3 sides. I squeege a strip across the middle from front to back first, then work the top half up, the bottom half down. Sounds lots harder than it is.||||reg||1
